screen.LIGHTING=Lighting
screen.WATER=Water
screen.TEXELS=Texel Shading
screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
option.SUN_BRIGHTNESS=Sun Brightness
option.TORCH_BRIGHTNESS=Torch Brightness
option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.WATER_CLARITY=Water Clarity
option.WATER_CLARITY.comment=How far you see into water. Lower is murkier.
option.WATER_SURFACE_OPACITY=Water Surface Opacity
option.WATER_SURFACE_OPACITY.comment=How much of the surface is the water's colour, however shallow.
option.GOD_RAY_STEPS=God Ray Steps
option.REFLECTION_STEPS=Reflection Steps
option.REFLECTION_SAMPLES=Reflection Samples
option.REFLECTION_SAMPLES.comment=Frames a water reflection averages over. More is smoother when still; fewer trails less when moving. 1 is off.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.REFLECTION_RES=Reflection Resolution
option.REFLECTION_RES.comment=The fraction of the screen water reflections are traced at.
value.REFLECTION_RES.1=Full
value.REFLECTION_RES.2=1/2
value.REFLECTION_RES.3=1/3
value.REFLECTION_RES.4=1/4
option.VOLUMETRIC_RES=Light Shaft Resolution
option.VOLUMETRIC_RES.comment=The fraction of the screen fog and light shafts are marched at.
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.1=Full
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.2=1/2
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.3=1/3
value.VOLUMETRIC_RES.4=1/4
option.SCALED_RESOLVE=Scaled Effects
option.SCALED_RESOLVE.comment=How reduced-resolution effects return to full resolution: a smooth, edge-aware upsample, or a crisp ordered dither.
value.SCALED_RESOLVE.0=Upsample
value.SCALED_RESOLVE.1=Dither
option.TEXEL_FULL_DISTANCE=Full Texel Distance
option.TEXEL_FULL_DISTANCE.comment=Blocks from you that shade at full detail, 16 texels per block. Past it, shading gets coarser in rings.
option.TEXEL_RING_WIDTH=Texel Ring Width
option.TEXEL_RING_WIDTH.comment=How many blocks wide each coarser ring is. Each ring halves the texels per block.
option.TEXEL_MIN_RES=Minimum Texels
option.TEXEL_MIN_RES.comment=The fewest texels per block far surfaces shade at.
option.TEXEL_DENOISE=Texel Denoise
option.TEXEL_DENOISE.comment=How many points across each coarse texel its shadow averages. More is steadier under leaves and plants, at more shadow lookups far away. 1 is off.
option.TEXEL_DENOISE_RES=Denoise Threshold
option.TEXEL_DENOISE_RES.comment=Texels this coarse or coarser are denoised, in texels per block. Finer texels shade at a single point, in real time.
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL=Temporal Denoise
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL.comment=Frames of history the coarsest texels' shadows average over, with new points scattered across the texel every frame; finer texels keep less (half per step), so they follow moving shadows more closely. Steadier under swaying plants and kelp, with a slight trail on fast shadows. 0 is off.
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL_POINTS=Temporal Points
option.TEXEL_TEMPORAL_POINTS.comment=Points each denoised texel takes a frame while the history averages them. More converges faster, at more shadow lookups.
